WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:15.968
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:16.238 --> 01:17.308
Oh, right.

3
01:17.308 --> 01:22.184
Miyata, have you decided who to ask for next month's column?

4
01:22.184 --> 01:25.048
I have someone in mind, so I'm setting up a meeting.

5
01:25.048 --> 01:26.362
Okay.

6
01:27.771 --> 01:34.219
Man, Director Tanabe said to get someone at Professor Iwanaga's level,

7
01:34.219 --> 01:35.603
but it's not easy, huh?

8
01:36.816 --> 01:39.013
Oh, right.

9
01:39.013 --> 01:42.085
Did you prepare the contract termination paperwork for the professor?

10
01:43.066 --> 01:45.967
We've been emailing, so the contents are settled.

11
01:45.967 --> 01:50.581
Okay. Then can you just get his seal in person?

12
01:50.581 --> 01:51.723
What?

13
01:51.723 --> 01:55.699
We owe Professor Iwanaga a lot, after all.

14
01:55.699 --> 01:59.269
And I'm sure you'd like to see him one last time too.

15
01:59.269 --> 02:00.269
Right?

16
02:57.162 --> 03:01.264
That's the end of our contract termination paperwork.

17
03:24.807 --> 03:29.409
Thank you very much for everything over the years.

18
03:41.197 --> 03:42.197
Likewise.

19
04:27.648 --> 04:28.861
Goodbye.

20
04:44.595 --> 04:46.503
Hey, you damn bitch.

21
04:50.726 --> 04:51.726
"Damn"?

22
04:55.947 --> 04:57.014
What is it?

23
04:59.679 --> 05:01.509
How dare you, of all people...

24
05:03.678 --> 05:06.254
make the professor cry, you nobody.

25
05:09.256 --> 05:10.387
You damn bitch.

26
05:12.518 --> 05:16.207
Drowning in your own inferiority complex,

27
05:16.207 --> 05:19.253
unable to notice the huge love right in front of you.

28
05:21.557 --> 05:24.394
What a thick-headed editor.

29
05:27.580 --> 05:30.147
I'll pretend I didn't hear that.

30
05:41.415 --> 05:45.775
Professor Iwanaga's column has ended,

31
05:45.775 --> 05:50.856
so I've come to ask if you might take over as his successor, Professor Hibino.

32
05:50.856 --> 05:53.003
You traveled to Osaka for this?

33
05:53.003 --> 05:54.003
Yes.

34
05:57.644 --> 06:00.136
Are you hoping that I, who tried to come between you two,

35
06:01.153 --> 06:04.710
would take this on out of guilt?

36
06:05.984 --> 06:08.042
No, um...

37
06:08.042 --> 06:09.333
You two broke up, huh?

38
06:12.671 --> 06:17.321
I don't need to feel guilty about it, right?

39
06:18.495 --> 06:19.892
Can we move past that?

40
06:22.967 --> 06:26.288
This kind of essay writing isn't my thing.

41
06:28.127 --> 06:30.474
Would you please at least consider it?

42
06:32.964 --> 06:34.815
Iwanaga was the right person.

43
06:37.565 --> 06:41.267
Ending things with him was a mistake.

44
07:44.178 --> 07:46.061
You left something.

45
07:50.550 --> 07:53.629
I want to give it to you. Can we meet up?

46
07:56.836 --> 07:59.977
I'll be at the park by the pier tomorrow.

47
08:04.091 --> 08:06.678
I'm sorry about the other day.

48
08:07.858 --> 08:11.132
No, I'm embarrassed for not realizing it.

49
08:13.712 --> 08:16.551
That you were Takashi's lover.

50
08:18.795 --> 08:20.987
That's all in the past now.

51
08:25.570 --> 08:26.570
Miyata.

52
08:27.830 --> 08:28.830
Yes?

53
08:30.189 --> 08:33.897
To be honest, I saw you back in college.

54
08:35.692 --> 08:36.692
Huh?

55
08:40.069 --> 08:44.090
I met Takashi in my first year of college.

56
08:57.183 --> 08:59.987
Back then, Takashi was always alone.

57
08:59.987 --> 09:03.736
He looked like he'd been abandoned by everyone in the world.

58
09:06.933 --> 09:13.033
I'm totally lost in our next statistics class. Could you teach me?

59
09:19.452 --> 09:21.483
I survived the year thanks to you.

60
09:22.507 --> 09:23.810
It's not much,

61
09:26.109 --> 09:27.593
but here's a thank-you.

62
09:27.593 --> 09:29.859
What? Can I open it?

63
09:29.859 --> 09:30.859
Go ahead.

64
09:32.306 --> 09:33.306
Thanks.

65
09:34.699 --> 09:35.927
- Can I put it on? - Yeah.

66
09:37.150 --> 09:38.150
Thanks.

67
09:41.463 --> 09:44.597
Hey, is this a matching set?

68
09:44.597 --> 09:46.133
Yeah, we're matching.

69
09:47.452 --> 09:50.127
Thanks. I'll treasure it.

70
09:50.127 --> 09:51.207
It looks great on you.

71
10:05.772 --> 10:06.772
Hey...

72
10:11.463 --> 10:15.163
Takashi told me everything about his past.

73
10:16.034 --> 10:19.466
That he was put up for adoption, that he changed his name,

74
10:20.770 --> 10:23.661
and about you too.

75
10:46.508 --> 10:47.400
You mean a trip?

76
10:47.400 --> 10:52.238
Yeah, like the beach, or a hot spring.

77
10:52.238 --> 10:54.570
We never get a day off.

78
10:54.570 --> 10:56.341
Sounds good.

79
10:56.341 --> 10:59.529
If it's a hot spring, I want a place with a pretty night view.

80
11:00.408 --> 11:03.550
We'll take a walk at night and talk until morning.

81
11:03.550 --> 11:04.942
Talk until morning?

82
11:25.047 --> 11:28.508
I'd never seen that expression on his face before.

83
11:29.738 --> 11:34.946
That was the first time I saw him actually in love.

84
11:40.778 --> 11:41.778
Takashi...

85
11:43.743 --> 11:45.657
is always thinking about you.

86
12:10.173 --> 12:14.068
I always thought I was the one chasing after you.

87
12:15.550 --> 12:17.702
And I was the only one getting jealous.

88
12:23.112 --> 12:28.247
But you felt the same way about me.

89
12:40.680 --> 12:41.927
Senpai, wait!

90
12:45.163 --> 12:46.163
Miyata?

91
12:50.851 --> 12:54.515
I came to get what I had left behind.

92
12:59.748 --> 13:01.027
What did I leave?

93
13:03.934 --> 13:04.934
It's me.

94
13:09.127 --> 13:10.676
You left me behind.

95
13:12.473 --> 13:13.921
First, at the station.

96
13:15.804 --> 13:18.134
The second time, in the apartment we shared.

97
13:23.908 --> 13:27.735
I'm not strong enough to endure it over and over either.

98
13:30.653 --> 13:31.733
Neither am I.

99
13:32.877 --> 13:35.237
You said you couldn't believe me.

100
13:38.861 --> 13:39.922
Why?

101
13:43.047 --> 13:45.627
I was scared of losing you again.

102
13:52.646 --> 13:54.694
I just heard from Arima...

103
13:57.057 --> 14:00.241
that you saw me once back in college.

104
14:02.124 --> 14:04.043
If you'd told me then,

105
14:06.220 --> 14:08.713
I could have believed in you...

106
14:10.723 --> 14:13.468
more easily than I do now.

107
14:15.210 --> 14:18.483
I was still young, and I was hurt.

108
14:20.513 --> 14:23.062
If you rejected me one more time,

109
14:24.877 --> 14:26.673
I don't think I could have taken it.

110
14:31.491 --> 14:33.763
Because you are that important to me.

111
14:35.976 --> 14:37.626
Me too.

112
14:37.626 --> 14:38.652
To me, you're...

113
14:41.749 --> 14:44.314
the one and only person in this world...

114
14:46.290 --> 14:48.174
that I truly love.

115
14:53.429 --> 14:54.570
Miyata.

116
15:00.140 --> 15:01.638
Tomorrow morning...

117
15:02.654 --> 15:04.247
and the morning after...

118
15:06.576 --> 15:08.566
and the thousands of mornings to come...

119
15:12.042 --> 15:13.687
I want to welcome them with you.

120
15:20.182 --> 15:22.775
Until both our lives come to an end.

121
15:28.991 --> 15:30.949
Can you be by my side?

122
15:38.565 --> 15:39.565
Yes.

123
15:41.749 --> 15:42.788
Forever,

124
15:44.245 --> 15:45.362
wherever we are,

125
15:47.972 --> 15:49.381
we'll be together.

126
15:53.618 --> 15:54.618
Takashi.

127
19:16.012 --> 19:18.736
Oh, the man of the hour.

128
19:18.736 --> 19:20.424
Thank you so much for this.

129
19:20.424 --> 19:22.115
Thank you.

130
19:22.115 --> 19:24.929
Look! Isn't it cute?

131
19:29.530 --> 19:31.584
Are you looking for someone?

132
19:31.584 --> 19:33.854
Oh, I'm not.

133
19:33.854 --> 19:35.515
Here, take one.

134
19:35.515 --> 19:37.128
Thank you.

135
19:46.260 --> 19:50.647
They stuck to their guns and persuaded the company.

136
19:50.647 --> 19:53.589
Miyata's got guts, huh?

137
19:54.745 --> 19:58.899
Well, Tokyo Business probably didn't want to make an enemy out of Takashi either.

138
20:00.274 --> 20:02.863
This Biz-Bear is Miyata, right?

139
20:05.080 --> 20:09.678
I can't believe the day has come when I'd lose to Miyata in cuteness.

140
20:09.678 --> 20:12.078
He actually brought your design to life,

141
20:12.078 --> 20:14.970
so you've got to give him credit.

142
20:16.155 --> 20:17.118
Okay.

143
20:17.118 --> 20:18.118
Good answer.

144
20:19.710 --> 20:21.256
Congratulations.

145
20:21.256 --> 20:22.256
Thanks.

146
20:24.433 --> 20:28.836
In the end, it ended up being published by us. I'm sorry.

147
20:28.836 --> 20:30.015
What are you saying?

148
20:30.015 --> 20:33.569
I helped too. Don't leave me out at the very end.

149
20:36.111 --> 20:39.412
Professor, it's almost time for your speech.

150
20:39.412 --> 20:40.412
Okay.

151
20:42.695 --> 20:43.849
You too, Miyata.

152
20:43.849 --> 20:44.849
Okay.

153
20:47.331 --> 20:51.501
[Takashi Iwanaga's "Searching for Tomorrow's Value" Book Launch Party]

154
20:56.590 --> 20:59.293
Thank you all for coming today.

155
21:00.131 --> 21:02.229
There were many twists and turns,

156
21:02.229 --> 21:08.151
but we've finally managed to publish "Searching for Tomorrow's Value".

157
21:11.063 --> 21:15.538
This book was made possible by working side by side with my editor, Miyata.

158
21:15.538 --> 21:19.607
I sincerely hope it will be loved for a long time.

159
21:24.294 --> 21:27.454
And there's one more thing I'd like to share.

160
21:29.703 --> 21:33.317
What came true wasn't just the book.

161
21:47.076 --> 21:52.811
Miyata and I have happily become life partners.

162
21:52.811 --> 21:53.988
- Huh? - What?

163
21:53.988 --> 21:55.907
Ooh la la!

164
22:02.288 --> 22:06.653
For the rest of our lives, we'll support and live alongside each other.

165
22:10.254 --> 22:11.813
Congratulations!

166
22:14.187 --> 22:15.187
Congratulations!

167
22:21.757 --> 22:22.757
Go, Miyata!

168
22:53.065 --> 22:58.335
I kind of wanted to see that condo you signed for, just once.

169
22:58.335 --> 23:01.043
I haven't canceled it yet.

170
23:01.043 --> 23:02.368
What?

171
23:02.368 --> 23:04.838
I thought you might change your mind.

172
23:05.684 --> 23:06.684
I see.

173
23:07.804 --> 23:09.183
Want to stay there tonight?

174
23:10.593 --> 23:12.460
Hmm...

175
23:12.460 --> 23:15.915
Now that we've exchanged eternal vows, you and me...

176
23:17.713 --> 23:20.303
But I don't have anything with me.

177
23:20.303 --> 23:23.838
And if I mess up the place, we can't return it, right?

178
23:23.838 --> 23:25.776
Who knows?

179
23:25.776 --> 23:27.690
Did you even read the contract?

180
23:27.690 --> 23:28.690
I skimmed it.

181
23:29.825 --> 23:32.698
Rich kids are all like this.

182
23:32.698 --> 23:34.747
You're so serious, Miyata.
